  "api": "aiplatform.v1",
  "service": "Vertex AI",
  "title": "Vertex AI: Agent Identity, Memory, Notebook Defaults, and API Rollbacks",
  "summary": "This update introduces breaking changes by making several agent-related schema properties read-only and removing recently added parameters. On the feature side, Vertex AI Agents gain significant new configuration options for identity, memory, encryption, and persona. A new method allows setting default Notebook Runtime Templates, and GenAI models get new capabilities like Bash code execution and video upscaling.",
  "details": "This release includes several breaking changes. The `idpNonce` parameter has been removed from `projects.locations.agents.create`, rolling back its recent addition. Similarly, the `ids` parameter has been removed from `projects.locations.publishers.files.list`, also rolling back a recent addition. The `parent` parameter for the new `projects.locations.notebookRuntimeTemplates.setDefault` method is now strictly required. Additionally, several properties related to agent status and identity have been made read-only: `status` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Agent`, `gaiaId` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentIdentity`, and `deleteTime`, `state`, `suspensionReason` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentStatus`, along with `reason` and `suspensionTime` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentStatusSuspensionReason`. Developers should adjust their code to reflect these removals and read-only constraints.\n\nOn the feature front, Vertex AI Agents receive substantial enhancements. The `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Agent` schema now includes new fields for `agentIdentity` (configuring the agent's principal identity), `memoryConfig` (agent-wide memory settings including `disableMemory`), `encryptionSpec` (CMEK for user data), `owner` (human owner), `persona` (agent's presentation), and `allowedTeammates` (outbound contact permissions). These additions provide much finer-grained control over agent behavior and security.\n\nA new method, `projects.locations.notebookRuntimeTemplates.setDefault`, is now available, allowing you to programmatically set a default Notebook Runtime Template for a given location.\n\nGenerative AI capabilities also see updates: code execution tools now support `BASH` as a language option in `GenaiVertexV1CodeExecutionCallContentCodeExecutionCallArguments` and `GenaiVertexV1CodeExecutionCallStepCodeExecutionCallStepArguments`. Video generation tasks can now perform `UPSCALE` operations via `GenaiVertexV1VideoConfig.properties.task`. Interaction statuses now include `REQUIRES_CONTINUATION` in `GenaiVertexV1Interaction` and `GenaiVertexV1InteractionStatusUpdate`, indicating multi-turn interactions. Finally, `GenaiVertexV1InteractionUsage` gains `initialInputTokens` for more detailed usage tracking.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "AI Platform",
    "Vertex AI",
    "Agents",
    "Notebooks",
    "Generative AI",
    "Breaking Change",
